 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [Terrain Raymarching](1357-terrain-raymarching.md)
-Terrain Raymarching renders a 2D heightmap $H(x, z)$ as a 3D surface. It differs from standard SDF ray marching because it does not strictly rely on the Lipschitz continuity of a global 3D SDF for step sizing; instead, it samples the heightmap at the ray's $(x, z)$ coordinates and checks if the ray's $y$ position intersects the height. It is chosen for efficient, infinite terrain rendering where vertical resolution is decoupled from horizontal sampling.
