+
+### [Neon Raymarcher](4157-neon-raymarcher.md)
+Neon Raymarcher generates an infinite procedural synthwave city using SDFs within a single fullscreen fragment shader, requiring no meshes or scene graph. It distinguishes itself by employing a deterministic integer-hashing contract shared between CPU and GPU to generate building layouts, and an analytic sine-wave curve to define the road centerline, ensuring perfect synchronization between the rendered visual and the camera path. [4157-neon-raymarcher]
+
+### [Menger Sponge Raymarching](4875-menger-sponge-raymarching.md)
+Menger Sponge Raymarching renders the Menger sponge fractal by iteratively applying a recursive distance function. It distinguishes itself by using a specific iterative modulo-based SDF construction that efficiently approximates the infinite-detail sponge geometry within a bounded volume, combined with a floor plane for grounding. [4875-menger-sponge-raymarching]
 
 ### [Fractals and Mathematical Surfaces](10024-fractals-and-mathematical-surfaces.md)
-This topic covers the generation of complex, self-similar, or chaotic surfaces using iterative mathematical functions (e.g., Mandelbulb, Julia sets) or recursive SDF compositions. It is chosen when the geometry requires infinite detail or organic complexity that cannot be described by simple Boolean primitives.
