 ### [Signed Distance Field Representations and Operations](13339-signed-distance-field-representations-and-operations.md)
-This foundational topic defines the exact analytical primitives (spheres, boxes, cylinders, cones) and the algebraic rules for combining them. It is distinct from [k-SDF](9530-k-sdf.md) approximations by providing exact Euclidean distances. It serves as the base layer for [SDF Primitive Definitions](1578-sdf-primitive-definitions.md) and [SDF Transformations](11027-sdf-transformations.md).
+This foundational topic defines the exact analytical primitives and the algebraic rules for combining them. It is distinct from k-SDF approximations by providing exact Euclidean distances. It serves as the base layer for SDF primitive definitions and transformations. [13339-signed-distance-field-representations-and-operations]
+
+### [Parametric Surface Density Model](14736-parametric-surface-density-model.md)
+The Parametric Surface Density Model defines a 3D object by six scalar quantities: three separating surfaces and the density fields defined on these interfaces. It solves the problem of reconstructing volumetric objects from limited data by explicitly modeling boundaries and material properties, rather than storing a dense 3D grid. Unlike siblings relying on implicit distance fields or voxel grids, it separates geometric definition from volumetric definition, allowing for adaptive elliptic operators to fill the volume. [14736-parametric-surface-density-model]
 
