 ### Infinite Floor Projection
 **Definition**: Renders an infinite textured floor by projecting screen coordinates into world space using perspective division, then applying player rotation and a checkerboard pattern [S4, unofficial].
-**Step**: Calculate lookAngle = -player.lookAngle * 6.2, clamped to SCR_HEIGHT. Compute moveVertical = player.z / 16.0, clamped to 0.0001 if zero. Loop y from yStart to yEnd, x from -SCR_WIDTH_HALF to SCR_WIDTH_HALF. Compute z = y + lookAngle (clamped to 0.0001). Calculate fx = x / z * moveVertical, fy = 200 / z * moveVertical. Rotate: rx = fx * sin(angle) - fy * cos(angle) + player.y/60.0, ry = fx * cos(angle) + fy * sin(angle) - player.x/60.0. Mirror negatives: if rx < 0 rx = -rx + 1; if ry < 0 ry = -ry + 1. Cull if rx <= 0 || ry <= 0 || rx >= 5 || ry >= 5. Draw red if rx%2 == ry%2, else blue [S4, unofficial].
