 **Parameter**: moveVertical scaling factor: 16.0 (derived from player.z / 16.0) [S4, unofficial]. Look angle multiplier: 6.2 (approximates 2π) [S4, unofficial].
 
 ## Background
 The use of FBM for hypertextures was formalized in research such as [S1], enabling the combination of analytical shapes with procedural noise. The "wing problem" and span-based un-bending techniques were developed to handle thin, dynamic structures like butterfly wings, as documented in [S3, unofficial]. Infinite floor projections are common in raycasting engines like those found in [S4, unofficial].
